# netsurf: github.com's React file list renders -- selector lists past 8
# alternatives, HTMLElement on every polyfill run, a minimal Shadow DOM
# (patch 242)
# Generated 2026-10-11
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 241)
#
# github.com/<repo> scored 64.7 (text 0.645) with 0 JS errors: its file
# list's commit messages and the latest-commit box are filled in by the
# <react-app app-name="code-view"> element, and that element was never
# upgraded, so React never booted. Found by probing the live page in the
# simulator (scorecard run_sim + a custom SIM_EVAL_JS):
#
#  - The upgrade sweep queries every defined name in one list (75 on
#    github.com). The native matcher keeps at most 8 alternatives of a
#    list (QJS_SEL_MAX_LIST: a stack array of ~7 KB structs, not safely
#    growable on the Vita) and dropped the rest without a word; react-app
#    was past the 8th. The querySelector(All) wrappers (patch 178) now send
#    a longer plain list to the native matcher in chunks of 8 and merge the
#    results in document order.
#  - The bridge installs its own HTMLElement again after the polyfill's
#    first run, so classes defined by the page extended the bridge's and
#    not 240's upgrade-aware constructor. That constructor is now installed
#    on every run (state on the hidden registry object, like 240's
#    createElement wrapper). A constructor that throws during an upgrade
#    is logged with its stack.
#  - React's components then reached Element.attachShadow, which the
#    engine lacks: github.com's invoker-commands polyfill wraps
#    HTMLElement.prototype.attachShadow unconditionally and called the
#    missing original (<relative-time>, <tool-tip>: "cannot read property
#    'call' of undefined"). A minimal Shadow DOM API: attachShadow
#    (open / closed, a second call throws NotSupportedError),
#    element.shadowRoot, a ShadowRoot (a document fragment with host,
#    mode, innerHTML, getElementById, adoptedStyleSheets) replacing the
#    interface census's empty ShadowRoot stub, and replaceChildren on
#    fragments. The shadow tree is NOT drawn -- the host's light DOM stays
#    what is rendered (the safe side for text).
#
# Gates: JS-selector-list-long.html LONGLIST 4/4 (Chromium 4/4; chunking
# disarmed 0/4), JS-attach-shadow.html SHADOW 7/7 (Chromium 7/7).
# github.com (r19's Chrome reference, with patch 243): 64.7 -> 81.8, text
# 0.645 -> 1.0, 0 JS errors.
#
